<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Review methodology</span><h1>How we research software reviews and alternatives</h1><p>Our comparisons start with the reader's workflow, then verify product facts and explain the limits of the evidence.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container policy-copy"><div class="tool-content"><h2>1. Define the decision</h2><p>We identify the main job, target user, switching reason and constraints before choosing products. A popular tool is not included when it cannot replace the relevant part of the workflow.</p><h2>2. Verify the original product</h2><p>We confirm the product identity, current scope, supported platforms, plan structure, pricing basis, export options and important restrictions from official sources.</p><h2>3. Select credible alternatives</h2><p>Candidates are chosen for differentiated use cases, not artificial variety. An option that replaces only one component is described as a partial alternative. Labels such as free, cheapest or best are used only when the relevant conditions can be supported.</p><h2>4. Check every material claim</h2><p>Prices include billing cadence, currency and plan context where available. We check device limits, seat minimums, usage allowances, integrations, migration and security claims when they affect the decision. Unknown or inaccessible details are stated rather than guessed.</p><h2>5. Separate research from testing</h2><p>Most ToolboxKart comparisons are documentation-based research. They do not claim hands-on testing unless test notes record the date, plan, platform, method and limitations. We do not publish fabricated ratings, reviews, benchmarks or customer outcomes.</p><h2>6. Explain tradeoffs and migration</h2><p>Each recommendation should say who it fits, who should skip it, what the reader gives up and what may need rebuilding. We prefer a practical acceptance checklist over a universal winner.</p><h2>7. Keep sponsorship separate</h2><p>Paid listings, if accepted, are clearly labeled and do not purchase an editorial ranking. See the <a href="/advertising-disclosure">advertising disclosure</a> for the commercial policy.</p></div></div></section><?php require __DIR__.'/includes/footer.php';?>
